WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.926
[MUSIC]

00:00:07.931 --> 00:00:12.679
SPEAKER: Suppose a rare
stradivarius violin is up for sale.

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:17.745
The bidding comes down to two
people, the greatest violinist

00:00:17.745 --> 00:00:22.675
in the world who wants to play
the magnificent instrument

00:00:22.677 --> 00:00:25.808
and the wealthiest
person in the world who

00:00:25.808 --> 00:00:29.001
wants to put it on display in a museum.

00:00:29.001 --> 00:00:35.391
Now, suppose the wealthy person out
bids the violinist and wins the auction.

00:00:35.395 --> 00:00:38.586
Would you say that this outcome is just?

00:00:38.586 --> 00:00:43.506
In that the person who pays the most
deserves to own the stradivarius.

00:00:43.507 --> 00:00:47.951
Or, would you say that this
outcome come is unjust?

00:00:47.951 --> 00:00:51.852
In that the person who can make
the best use of the stradivarius

00:00:51.852 --> 00:00:54.362
is the one who deserves to have it.

00:00:54.362 --> 00:00:58.362
[MUSIC]

